"suggestion":"1. Establish a clear focal hierarchy: Make the puzzle board the undeniable primary focal point by increasing its scale, adding a subtle glow or border to lift it from the background, and increasing the contrast between the floor tiles and the walls. 2. Demote the HUD: Reduce the visual weight of the Level/Moves/Par/Time boxes by using a smaller font, lower contrast, and a more compact layout in the top-right corner. 3. Clarify the objective: Move the objective text into a more compact, less glowing banner or integrate it into the HUD to stop it from competing with the board. 4. Improve board legibility: Increase the size and contrast of the player, crate, and goal icons. Make the gate visually distinct from the walls (e.g., a different color or a clear opening). 5. Fix the reading flow: Move the controls legend closer to the board, perhaps as a sidebar or a collapsible panel, to create a tighter, more logical grouping of information. 6. Clarify the lever-gate relationship: Replace the decorative line with a clear, labeled indicator or a subtle animation that shows the connection, or add a small icon on the gate that lights up when the lever is pulled."
}

