"critique":"The board's visual language is internally inconsistent and lacks the precision of a production system. 1) The wall tiles are rendered as a dense, noisy texture of vertical slats that reads as a rendering artifact or unfinished placeholder rather than a deliberate material; this texture is too high-frequency and visually competes with the game entities. 2) The 'lever' is depicted as a thin, glowing diagonal line that violates the grid-based geometry of the game, appearing to float over the tiles and lack a clear base or anchor point. 3) The 'pressure plate' is a small, glowing teal circle that is visually disconnected from the grid cell it occupies, lacking the solid, grounded feel of the crate or player. 4) The HUD cards (Level, Moves, Par, Time) have inconsistent internal alignment; the icons are not vertically centered with the text, and the spacing between the icon and the label/value is uneven. 5) The 'Objective' banner has a gradient that fades to a solid color, but the transition is abrupt and the text alignment within the banner is not perfectly centered relative to the icon.",
"suggestion":"1) Redesign the wall tiles to use a cleaner, more geometric pattern (e.g., a subtle bevel or a simple grid line) that reinforces the grid structure without visual noise. 2) Reconstruct the lever as a solid, grid-aligned object with a clear base and a handle that rotates within the cell, using a consistent material and color palette. 3) Redesign the pressure plate to be a flat, grid-filling element with a subtle inset or glow that clearly occupies the cell, matching the visual weight of the crate. 4) Standardize the HUD card layout: ensure all icons are vertically centered with their corresponding text, and use a consistent spacing scale (e.g., 8px or 12px) between elements. 5) Refine the 'Objective' banner by using a more subtle gradient or a solid background with a border, and ensure the text is perfectly centered relative to the icon and the banner's overall width."
